10
00:52:36,521 --> 00:52:42,521
The Equalizer 2 (also promoted as The Equalizer II and EQ2) is a 2018
American vigilante action-thriller film directed by Antoine Fuqua.

11
00:57:52,173 --> 00:57:58,173
It is the sequel to the 2014 film The Equalizer, which was based on the TV series of the
same name, as well as the second installment of The Equalizer trilogy.

12
01:03:07,826 --> 01:03:13,826
The film stars Denzel Washington in the lead role, Pedro Pascal, Ashton Sanders,
Melissa Leo, Bill Pullman, and Orson Bean in his final film role.

13
01:08:23,478 --> 01:08:29,478
It follows Marine Corps veteran and retired DIA officer Robert McCall as he
sets out on a path of revenge after an associate is murdered.

14
01:13:39,130 --> 01:13:45,130
The film is the fourth collaboration between Washington and Fuqua, following Training Day (2001), The Equalizer (2014), and
The Magnificent Seven (2016), and marks the first time Washington has starred in a sequel to one of his films.

15
01:18:54,782 --> 01:19:00,782
Talks of a sequel began seven months before the first film was released.

16
01:24:10,434 --> 01:24:16,434
The project was officially announced in April 2015.

17
01:29:26,086 --> 01:29:32,086
Filming began in September 2017 and took place in
Boston and other areas in Massachusetts.

18
01:34:41,739 --> 01:34:47,739
The Equalizer 2 was released in the United States on
July 20, 2018, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

19
01:39:57,391 --> 01:40:03,391
The film received mixed reviews and was a commercial success, like
its predecessor, grossing $190 million worldwide.

20
01:45:13,043 --> 01:45:19,043
Another sequel, The Equalizer 3, was released on September 1, 2023.

21
01:50:28,695 --> 01:50:34,695
The film explores themes of drug dealer, martial arts, central
intelligence agency (cia), rape, kidnapping.

22
01:55:44,347 --> 01:55:50,347
The tone is intense.
